{
  "problem_description": "Perform dimensional analysis for Rayleigh-Bénard convection in a planar horizontal layer of fluid heated from below, to derive the dimensionless form of the Nusselt number (denoted as Nu). \nThis analysis uses ONLY the following 7 physical quantities as input parameters: \nthe height of the container (h), the thermal conductivity (lambda), the temperature difference between the top and bottom surfaces (delta_T), the gravitational acceleration (g), the thermal expansion coefficient (alpha), the kinematic viscosity (nu), and the thermal diffusivity (kappa).",
  "analyzed_output_var": "Nu",
  "analyzed_output_reasoning": "The Nusselt number Nu is a dimensionless measure of convective heat transfer. Using the provided seven input physical quantities (h, delta_T, lambda, g, alpha, nu, kappa) one can form the Rayleigh number Ra and the Prandtl number Pr to nondimensionalize heat transport. Ra = (g * alpha * delta_T * h^3) / (nu * kappa) is dimensionless and Pr = nu / kappa is dimensionless; Nu is then expressed as a dimensionless function Nu = F(Ra, Pr). Given that Nu is dimensionless, the dimensionless analysis confidence is high.",
  "analyzed_output_confidence": "high",
  "analyzed_input_vars": [
    "h",
    "delta_T",
    "lambda",
    "g",
    "alpha",
    "nu",
    "kappa"
  ],
